        "procedure": "Under aerobic conditions, an orange solution of (NH4)2[Ce(NO3)6] (5.5 g, 10.0 mmol) in H2O/HO2CMe (19/6 mL) was slowly added to a stirred pale yellow-brown solution of Mn(NO3)2·xH2O (0.90 g, 5.0 mmol) and bpy (0.78 g, 5.0 mmol) in H2O/HO2CMe (50/15 mL), giving a dark greenish-brown solution. The volume was reduced by 60% by rotary evaporation at 40 °C, then the solution was left undisturbed at ambient temperature. After 24 h, dark greenish-brown crystals of 1·2H2O were collected by filtration, washed with cold acetone (2 × 7 mL) and Et2O (2 × 7 mL), and dried in vacuo.",
